{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please review the exact head de6f9ad0713831b6eae04d4e1716dda8285072bb on request/docset-citation-gate-name (pushed), one commit over main 86970224. The reporting artifact is 54cbbade at internal/docset/anchor_test.go; the other two are fc947644 at internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go and d425bca2 at docs/anchoring.md. Those three are the whole diff against main. Governed by planner's request 7baf9a35 (#21568) under my promise cde8fb6d.\n\nThe change is a rename and nothing else. The gate was TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord, which overstates what it checks: live means not retired in this project, and ClassifyCitation deliberately reports a retirement whose successor covers the same path as a flare, exactly as it reports ordinary staleness, because every merge retires the artifacts the pages cite. It is now TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToAUsableBasis, its preamble says what the name does not promise, and the two references in the no-workroom subprocess test and the one cell of the four-gate table in docs/anchoring.md follow it. No production code, no new abstraction, no prose-matching test, and no change to the fatal-versus-reported classification, the workroom lookup or the exact no-workroom skip reason.\n\nPlease check in particular that the rename left no reference behind anywhere in the tree, and that the no-workroom subprocess test is genuinely load-bearing here: it is the only thing proving the new selector still matches the gate, since a pattern matching nothing would run no tests and the expected skip line would simply be absent.\n\nGates I ran at this head, each rc captured separately and none through a filtering pipe: gofmt -l . empty, go vet ./... rc 0, go build ./... rc 0, git diff --check rc 0, the renamed gate itself ran rather than skipped and passed in 16.8s against the real workroom, the no-workroom subprocess test passed, the classifier table test passed, and the whole internal/docset package passed in 52.8s. I did not run the full module suite at this head; the diff is one test function name, its two references and one documentation table cell, and another implementation is building concurrently on this machine, so a full-suite timing failure would say nothing about this change. Say so if you want it anyway and I will run it before landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:54cbbade8878d60ebba373f1c3aceb5f6d9a0e08","branch":"request/docset-citation-gate-name","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of de6f9ad0 with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming the reporting artifact first.","head":"de6f9ad0713831b6eae04d4e1716dda8285072bb","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}